BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ironman703venicejesolo-w1-s4-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T164533Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261119
SUMMARY:○ BIKE RAMP TEST (40 min)
DESCRIPTION:BIKE RAMP TEST - Zwift on the D100 (ERG). Eat 2-3 h before\, 
 fan on\, bottle. Warm-up 10 min easy + 5 x 1 min at 100-110 rpm with 1 m
 in easy between. Then the test: stay seated at 85-95 rpm and ride until 
 you can't hold the cadence. FTP = 75% of the best 1-min power\; expect t
 o stop around 240-250 W. It sets the bike zones from week 2.\n\nWeek 1 o
 f 23 - Re-entry\nRE-ENTRY. Vertical jump comes back about 18 days after 
 an ultra\, which is Thursday\, so the running is all easy and the first 
 box jumps start low. Durability is the through-line of the whole block: 
 long sessions over 90 min are what preserve running economy under fatigu
 e\, which is the 70.3 run leg in one sentence.\n157 days to IRONMAN 70.3
  Venice-Jesolo.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ironman703venicejesolo-w1-s5-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T164533Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:◆ Strength LOWER (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Strength LOWER - HEAVY\, 45 min. Back squat 4 x 4 at 80 kg (7
 7.5 if 13 Nov's 75 x 5 was near max)\, safety pins on (75 x 5 on 13 Nov 
 puts the 1RM near 88-90 kg: 4 x 4 at 80 kg on 20 Nov\, then add 2.5 kg w
 hen the last set moves well). Hack squat if there's no rack or you're wr
 ecked. Then Bulgarian split squat 3 x 5/leg heavy\, single-leg calf rais
 es 3 x 8 loaded\, Nordic curls 2 x 4. COMPLEX PAIRING: after each heavy 
 set\, 5 box jumps or 20 m of bounds within 2 min - heavy resistance plus
  plyo beats either alone for running economy. Heavy loads at or above 90
 % 1RM give greater economy gains than lighter ones\, and the effect need
 s 10-14 weeks\, which is exactly this block. LOWER-LEG AND FOOT\, 5 min:
  tibialis anterior raises 3 x 15-20\, heel walks 2 x 20 m\, eccentric do
 rsiflexion 3 x 10\, short-foot holds 3 x 30 s per side.\n\nWeek 1 of 23 
 - Re-entry\nRE-ENTRY. Vertical jump comes back about 18 days after an ul
 tra\, which is Thursday\, so the running is all easy and the first box j
 umps start low. Durability is the through-line of the whole block: long 
 sessions over 90 min are what preserve running economy under fatigue\, w
 hich is the 70.3 run leg in one sentence.\n155 days to IRONMAN 70.3 Veni
 ce-Jesolo.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
