SUMMARY:◆ Legs
DESCRIPTION:Legs - maintenance + glute-med\, 30 min after iftar\, before 
 the 21:00 swim. LOWER-LEG AND FOOT\, about 5 min at the end: tibialis an
 terior raises 3 x 15-20 (heels on a step\, toes lifting)\, heel walks 2 
 x 20 m\, eccentric dorsiflexion 3 x 10 slow against a band\, short-foot 
 holds 3 x 30 s per side\, tennis ball under the arch 60 s. An 8-week RCT
  in amateur runners raised lactate threshold velocity 5.9% with intrinsi
 c foot work - but that was 30 min DAILY\, so treat this as maintaining t
 he tissue that failed on 7 Sep\, not as a 5.9% gain.\n\nWeek 14 of 23 - 
 Ramadan\nBuy the wetsuit now. Buy for BUOYANCY not speed - beginner suit
 s run 5 mm through core/hips/legs\, which directly fixes the sinking-leg
 s problem. Wetsuits give the biggest gain to inefficient low-buoyancy sw
 immers\, i.e. you: 5-11%\, roughly 2-4 min over 1.9 km. Also buy neopren
 e BOOTIES - legal below 18.3 C and the water will be 15-17 C. ABU DHABI 
